From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:10:14 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vkms: log the eye, MSA MISC1 and VSC SDP of each frame

A DisplayPort source tells the sink which eye each frame of a
frame-sequential stream carries: in the vertical blanking before the
frame, the Main Stream Attribute's MISC1 bits 2:1 say 11b for a left
eye, 01b for a right eye and 00b for no stereo (DisplayPort 1.1a, as
VESA's public DisplayPort 1.2 overview of December 2010 quotes it, and
as drm_dp.h defines DP_MSA_MISC_STEREO_*), and since DisplayPort 1.2 a
VSC SDP whose stereo interface byte, DB0, names the method, here frame
or field sequential with the eye named by MISC1 (0x01). VKMS has no
link, so a test could not check what a driver would signal with each
frame, only the pixels.

Give each CRTC a debugfs file, stereo_link, that lists its last 256
frames, one per line, the oldest first:

  frame=120 eye=left misc1=0x06 vsc=0x01 db0=0x01 scanout=4 wb=0

the frame's vblank count; its eye (none outside frame-sequential
modes); the MISC1 stereo bits the frame was announced with; the
revision of the VSC SDP sent with it, built with drm_dp_vsc_sdp_pack()
as a driver would (revision 0x1, "3D stereo only"; 0x00 when none is
sent, as outside frame-sequential modes) and its DB0; a number that
changes each time a commit that updates the planes takes effect, so a
test can see that both eyes of a pair show the same planes; and
whether the composer wrote the frame into a writeback buffer, which
ties a writeback job to its frame and eye.

VKMS now selects the DisplayPort helpers for the VSC SDP packer.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/Kconfig         |   2 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_composer.c |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_crtc.c     | 159 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/vkms/vkms_drv.h      |  51 +++++++++
 4 files changed, 213 insertions(+)

